  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to UNECA Business Plan 2014-2015</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the enhanced focus on trade and the right to economic and social development of Danish development policy, Denmark through this programme seeks a renewed partnership with UNECA based on the organisation&#xbf;s mandate and comparative advantages in the multilateral architecture in Africa.

The aim is to support UNECA in promoting social and economic development of its Member States, fostering intra-regional integration, and promoting international cooperation for Africa&#xbf;s development.

In partnership with DFID, Norway and Sweden, Denmark will provide joint funding to five activity areas of UNECA. The partnership will take the lead on regional integration and trade as well as social development policy. This aligns the support closely with Danish policy, as expressed in the Right to a Better Life, Opportunity Africa, Trademark East Africa, and the recommendations of the Africa Commission.</narrative>
  </description>
